## Purpose

With speculative decoding, `EngineCoreOutput.new_token_ids` can contain multiple accepted tokens. Today those tokens can be surfaced as one streaming chunk, which makes streaming cadence uneven and can make server-side speculative token settings observable through chunk size.

This split is done in the engine output processor because it already owns token IDs, detokenizer/logprob state, stop handling, and finish metadata; doing it in a gateway from text deltas would require extra tokenizer work and duplicate this state.

## Test Plan

For the baseline run, remove `--stream-output-token-by-token`; for the token-by-token run, keep it enabled.

```bash
vllm serve /model/DeepSeek-V4-Flash \
  --trust-remote-code \
  --kv-cache-dtype fp8 \
  --block-size 256 \
  -tp 8 \
  --tokenizer-mode deepseek_v4 \
  --tool-call-parser deepseek_v4 \
  --enable-auto-tool-choice \
  --reasoning-parser deepseek_v4 \
  --speculative-config '{
        "method": "mtp",
        "num_speculative_tokens": 3
    }' \
  --stream-output-token-by-token \
  --enable-prompt-tokens-details
```

```bash
curl -N -sS http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions   -H "Content-Type: application/json"   -d '{
    "model": "/model/DeepSeek-V4-Flash",
    "stream": true,
    "stream_options": {
      "include_usage": true,
      "continuous_usage_stats": true
    },
    "return_token_ids": true,
    "max_tokens": 64,
    "temperature": 0,
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Write a concise explanation of speculative decoding in three bullet points."
      }
    ]
  }'
```

